11
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:09,000
The Baxter is a 2005 American comedy film written by, directed
by and starring comedian Michael Showalter.

12
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
A "Baxter", as defined by the film, is the nice, dull guy in a romantic
comedy who is dumped at the end of the story for the protagonist.

13
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:15,000
Much light humor is made of showing Showalter as a "Baxter" in several typical romantic comedy clichés: being abandoned at the altar as a
former love is claimed by her high school sweetheart, and being left in college at a pep rally for an underdog sports hero.

14
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:48,000
The plot revolves around the life of Elliot Sherman during the two weeks before his wedding, as
he doggedly fights off the curse of his former Baxter role in relationships.

15
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
IFC Films financed the film and produced it with Plum Pictures.

16
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
They gave the film a very limited release; it had a U.S.

17
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:27,000
box office gross of $181,872.

18
01:21:54,000 --> 01:22:00,000
The film explores themes of love triangle, flashback, wedding, screwball comedy.

19
01:26:27,000 --> 01:26:33,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
